  "term": "Desensitization, Psychologic",
  "definition": "A psychological desensitization is a behavior therapy method that uses deep muscle relaxation while a person is exposed to anxiety-provoking situations in gradual steps. The relaxation is used to reduce or block the anxiety response to those stimuli.",
